>=20
> Hi SVEN,
>=20
> We shipped five major updates in September, including AI =
Discoverability in Site Audit <https://app.ahrefs.com/site-audit>, Page =
types in Site Explorer <https://app.ahrefs.com/site-explorer>, and more.
>=20
>  <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoWrVGjks_cI>
> Here's the blog post =
<https://ahrefs.com/blog/new-features-september-2026/> version if you =
prefer reading, or scroll on for the highlights. For the minor updates, =
check our changelog <https://ahrefs.com/blog/new-features/>.
>=20
> Site Explorer
>=20
> Organic pages by type
>=20
> The new Organic pages by type widget in the Overview =
<https://app.ahrefs.com/site-explorer> breaks down where a site's =
traffic comes from by page category, blog, tools, service pages, and =
more.
>=20
>=20
> Run it on a competitor to see which content types are really pulling =
their weight, then click any type to jump straight to those pages in the =
Top pages report.
>=20
> Site Audit
>=20
> AI Discoverability
>=20
> A new issue category <https://app.ahrefs.com/site-audit> checks =
whether AI crawlers from ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Google's AI answers =
can actually read and cite your pages.=20
>=20
>=20
> The first batch of issues covers:
>=20
> Pages blocked from AI bots in robots.txt
> Pages too slow or heavy for AI crawlers
> Inconsistent AI bot policies
> Pages requiring JavaScript rendering that most AI bots cannot read
> Keywords Explorer
>=20
> Semantic filters
>=20
> Instead of matching on exact words, semantic filters match by meaning, =
so researching a short or ambiguous term like a brand name returns =
relevant keywords without the noise of unrelated uses.=20
>=20
>=20
> The result is a cleaner keyword list with far less manual filtering.
>=20
> =20
> Watch our video <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoWrVGjks_cI> or =
read the full blog post =
<https://ahrefs.com/blog/new-features-september-2026/> for all the =
details.
